es he doesn't come  trying to kill you his tactics are way  more subtle this embodiment of evil is  often just someone who tempts us with  giving up our morals in order to get  what our heart desires that is very much  what the dark old represents and whilst  it corrupts wonder it also offers there  a better life  you break the rules look out  and become a hero  i do it i become the enemy  that doesn't seem fair he then gets its  claws and wonder which is why we find  her buried under rubble inside her mind  whilst the scarlet witch is showing up  at breakneck speeds in the film we  discover that every universe other than  the 616 has a version of her where she's  happy with her kids and every night  wonder goes to sleep dreaming of this  better life upon waking up she's faced  with a cold hard truth and even without  the dark hold you can see how this would  break someone mentally no wonder much  like age of ultron was first introduced  as a villain in the comics but over the  years we've watched her transform into a  hero before her power ended up proving  too much in stories like avengers  disassembled and house of m we've seen  how she's been someone who can do  exactly what she wants and therein lies  a downfall like silas stone says in zack  snyder's justice league the question no  the challenge  won't be doing it  it will be not doing  not seeing  wanda is one of if not the most powerful  person in the universe and therefore she  should be able to have what she wants  now her being the villain here makes the  perfect opposite to strange wander isn't  willing to sacrifice what she wants for  the greater good and she will happily  kill that on mother's day just cause  there'll be someone to look after the  kids jerk supposing this strange could  have had a happy life but instead he  sacrificed the time stone got dusted and  came back five years later having found  that the love of his life had moved on  to make things worse her husband is a  massive doctor strange fan and stephen  ends up having to stand at the wedding  pretending to be happy watching her walk  down the aisle wanda also tempts him  with another universe in which he can be  with christine but he turns this down as  the cost of killing america would be too  great for him it puts them at complete  opposite ends of the spectrum and shows  two powerful magic entities that could  both have what they want but they decide  for themselves to take different paths  just before they meet her comitage  wander says that it won't be her that  comes for america it'll be the scholar  witch so her showing up at comitage to  tempt steven when she never did this at  the forest is showing the extent of her  possession she's using the same tactics  that the darkhold used on her in order  to try and tempt steven with a better  life where he will finally obtain the  happiness that he lies about having now  wonder's design in the movie is based  heavily on a lot of horror villains the  samara from the ring whose infamous tv  crawl she imitates when exiting the  mirror dimension the wicked witch of the  west's horned forest trees that we  somewhat see at her home when the  illusion is broken elements of carry  with the oil all over her face  terminator when she limps along after  the heroes with her eyes glowing red  snow white which we even see playing on  a tv in other wonders home the exorcist  when she appears from the corner and  snaps x's neck and there's a lot of  references to past works it plans this  idea on her head that she's a classic  horror monster  who's completely unstoppable when we did  our analysis of the batman we talked  about how matt reeves lean into villains  like michael myers and jason voorhees in  order to give the idea to audiences that  batman was somewhat of a supernatural  being his slow walking was used to  intimidate those that he faced and  wonder very much pulls from these same  archetypes making her a one-dimensional  character also makes her a force of  nature and whenever strange and co  throughout her she has the ability to  get around it and bounce back from it  now i know there's a lot of criticism  about how the illuminati are handled in  this movie but personally i think that  what they do is brilliant to make us  realize just how powerful that wonder is  for years fans have cried out for not  only john krasinski to be fan cast as mr  fantastic but we've also been desperate  to see professor rex in the mcu these  are given to us in the film and just  when we think they're gonna save the day  they're ripped apart by wonder which  also rips our heart out in the audience  look look at me you can see the moment  my heart breaks into watching professor  rex get his neck broken now i think  everyone is going to have a kind of  knee-jerk reaction to it at first but  with the x-men and fantastic four both  getting movies in the future i think  it's safe to say that they'll be back  you will no doubt get them again and  those who hate this might even come to  appreciate how much of a nephew that it  is to fans a ralph boner showed us  fergie likes to troll and watching  warner drop the coldest lines i've ever  heard in a comic book movie just  elevates the scene so much she drops the  what mouth line in bit about sue storm  being that a race reads kids back to  back and it shows how she will no longer  let anyone stand in her way  i'm the smartest man alive  reed richards of the fantastic four  the world's smartest man  poses no more threat to me  than does its smartest termite  now though it's not really labeled as  search this film is very much a versus  movie we've had a number of them over  the years like godzilla vs kong batman v  superman alien vs predator and so on and  so on they're very much a staple of big  franchises and now i like them i have to  admit that at this point they all follow  the same sort of formula when godzilla  vs kong was getting filmed i think we  all knew that it would end with the pair  teaming up together in order to stop a  bigger threat that was actually behind  the scenes controlling it all most of  the movies in the genre and with the two  opposing teams putting their differences  to the side in order to fight a bigger  bad guy and this was even somewhat the  structure that marvel used for captain  america civil war many people even  expected a secret villain in this and  when those catholic monsters showed up  in the trailers it seemed like that was  what we were gonna get what multiverse  of madness does though is that it keeps  the scholar which is the main villain  and because of this it doesn't cheapen  her in the end the dark knight rises  show that you can often strip one of the  main talking points of your film if you  do a bait and switch at the end and i  think it's smart of marvel to just be  like nope wonder is the bad guy the film  ends with her coming face to face with  her children and a version of herself  which she ends up attacking this scares  her kid so much she realizes the monster  that she's become and lies through her  teeth saying that she didn't hurt anyone  she's then faced with a version of  herself who is the mother that she  should be rather than the person she's  become she tells her that they'll be  loved which finally breaks wonder and  makes her realize her wrongdoings even  in this moment scarlet witch is so  powerful that she can only be defeated  by herself and this strategy to take her  into the life she could have makes us  see where she's gone wrong at her core  wonder is still a hero even though we  just watched her brutally murder people  for two hours and over the last seven  years we've followed the growth of the  character as she's went from villain to  hero and back to being a villain she's  arguably been on the most complex arc  out of any mcu character and pushing her  over the deep end like this was not only  surprising but damn right divisive and  for a good reason we often don't want to  see the faults in the heroes that we  respect but watching her corrupted by  her selfish attitude very much acts as  an example to us of what not to do this  is also mirrored and strange who could  potentially be with a version of  christine at the end of the film but he  forgoes this because of the incursion  that it would cause strange is such a  hero in this moment because wanda has  been such a big villain throughout the  movie and then being at opposite sides  of the spectrum is the perfect way to  drive the narrative wonder very much  feels like she's a monster from an 80s  kids movie back before everything got  heavily sanitized and the horror she  brings in the film is used expertly to  tear off finer only the characters in  the movie but also us as an audience  it's masterful storytelling that allows  her to become the perfect villain that  this film needs and in the hands of  anyone else i think that wonder may have  under-delivered instead elizabeth olsen  completely knocks it out the park and  delivers what's probably her most  memorable performance in the mcu scarlet  witch was incredible and hopefully have  helped to make you appreciate the movie  a little bit more if you came out of it  not liking the choices they made  obviously i'd love to hear your thoughts  in the comments below so make sure you  drop them and just to let you know we're  running a competition right now and  giving away three copies of spider-man  now a home on the 15th of may all you  have to do to be on the chance of  winning is like the video make sure you  subscribe with notifications on and drop  a comment below with your thoughts on  the film the winners of last month's  competition are on screen right now so  if that's you then message me on twitter  at heavyspoilers if you want someone  else to watch them make sure you check  out our breakdown of the unanswered  questions in the movie which goes over a  lot of the things that people are very  confused about hopefully